"\nTARGET 24 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_25\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY e1f9ca90f5325330ed60f8181a0cb6cf9fd80e05 838e3ce12ad89b8f1e46f0b9616c2087122a28835cc86e98f6faa19a00922360 RANGES [[1, 41]] MASKED []\n1: # Work log \u2014 2026\u002d07\u002d25\n2: \n3: ## QA rev 2: discoverability + unconfigured\u002dstate UX + VM networking\n4: \n5: \u002d Cloud tools moved from Network Settings to Game Settings \u2192 CLOUD TOOLS;\n6:   backup entries renamed to the explicit To/From Device/Cloud names.\n7: \u002d Unconfigured rclone: Cloud Tools actions render dimmed (manual row,\n8:   alpha\u002ddimmed text color + makeAcceptInputHandler) and offer cloud_setup;\n9:   System Management cloud entries guard via requireCloud lambda (must be\n10:   captured in entry callbacks \u2014 caught by build).\n11: \u002d VM/QEMU: profile gains extra_forwards (host 15572 \u2192 guest 5572) so the\n12:   cloud web GUI works from the host browser; generic\u002dx64\u002dvm gains\n13:   \u002d\u002dnet bridged (+ \u002d\u002dbridge) for LAN\u002djoining QA; cloud_setup prints the\n14:   forward address when it detects 10.0.2.x slirp addressing.\n15: \u002d Image rebuilt + release dev\u002dgeneric_x64\u002d20260725 updated (rev 2 notes).\n16: \n17: ## backup vs back up: convention set and applied\n18: \n19: \u002d Rule: verb = \"back up\" (two words), noun/adjective = \"backup\". Swept our\n20:   surfaces: only the two new entry labels violated it (now BACK UP\n21:   CONFIGURATIONS TO DEVICE/CLOUD); dialogs, scripts, and docs were already\n22:   correct. Upstream's hidden \"BACKUP USER DATA\" left alone. Convention\n23:   recorded in es\u002dnative\u002dui.instructions.md; image rebuilt, release updated.\n24: \n25: ## Console\u002dfirst principle (maintainer rule)\n26: \n27: \u002d cloud_setup had QEMU/VM port\u002dforward guidance in product UI \u2014 removed; QA\n28:   guidance lives only in release notes/dev docs. Wording revamped phone\u002dfirst\n29:   (no browser exists on the handheld). Rule captured in\n30:   rclone\u002dcloud\u002dsync.instructions.md and es\u002dnative\u002dui.instructions.md: product\n31:   surfaces assume player + handheld + phone; QEMU is a test vehicle only.\n32: \n33: ## Console\u002dfirst rule automated in the pre\u002dpush guard\n34: \n35: \u002d The tester\u002donly VM hint lives solely in fork release notes (never code), so\n36:   upstream PRs can't carry it. To prevent future regressions, .githooks/\n37:   pre\u002dpush now content\u002dscans pr/* diffs of product\u002dsurface script dirs for\n38:   QEMU/VM/port\u002dforward/loopback wording and blocks the push. Verified: the\n39:   pre\u002dfix cloud_setup commit would have been blocked (2 hits); current\n40:   branches are clean (0 hits).\n\nTARGET 25 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_26\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 990436bd545db1a69f737b22d22cac5adf82939c 9d9853eb35d50694449aa5c7e8f8d83b63598d0f791737e2dee3b9c3769258db RANGES [[1, 41]] MASKED [17]\n1: # Work log \u2014 2026\u002d07\u002d26\n2: \n3: ## Conflict\u002dresolution milestone planned\n4: \n5: \u002d Created fork milestone \"Cloud Saves: Visual Conflict Resolution\"; rewrote\n6:   #11 as the epic; discrete tasks filed: #19 compatibility research,\n7:   #20 manifest design, #21 capture, #22 detection engine, #23 Vita\u002dstyle ES\n8:   wizard, #24 merge/re\u002dslot semantics, #25 V2 snapshots/rollback.\n9: \u002d Planning doc: plans/conflict\u002dresolution/vita\u002dstyle\u002dconflict\u002dresolution.md.\n10: \n11: ## Fresh\u002dhandheld journey (#26) implemented\n12: \n13: \u002d Epic #26 filed as the cloud program's acceptance test (precedes conflict\n14:   resolution). New: cloud_content_backup (mirror of restore; skips save/\n15:   backup dirs, skips empties), ES UPLOAD CONTENT TO CLOUD picker, RESTORE\n16:   EVERYTHING (journey marker survives the settings\u002drestore reboot; boot\n17: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n18:   EVERYTHING (backuptool + saves + forced system upload via ThreadedCloudSync).\n19: \u002d QA image rev 4 published. Next: two\u002dfresh\u002dVMs round\u002dtrip QA, then PR\n20:   assembly and the conflict\u002dresolution milestone.\n21: \n22: ## UTM boot\u002dhang triage: bridged\u002dby\u002ddefault reverted (profile v3)\n23: \n24: \u002d Reported: 20260726 UTM bundle \"never boots, just spins\" + looked ~100MB\n25:   smaller. Verified image healthy by booting the published qcow2 under KVM\n26:   (kernel 5s, sway+ES up, storage resized, cloud tools present); release\n27:   asset sizes identical across days \u002d> size delta was a truncated download.\n28: \u002d Root cause of the hang: rev 4 defaulted the UTM bundle to Bridged vmnet,\n29:   which fails/hangs on many macOS Wi\u002dFi hosts. Reverted default to\n30:   Shared/NAT (forwards: SSH loopback, web GUI LAN\u002dbound); Bridged is a\n31:   documented one\u002dclick opt\u002din. Also earlier: per\u002dbundle UUID/MAC fix.\n32: \u002d Lesson: VM profile changes need a boot check on the weakest host config\n33:   before release; NAT\u002ddefault + opt\u002din bridged is the safe posture.\n34: \n35: ## UTM bridged hang: root cause confirmed from user log\n36: \n37: \u002d Unified log showed `SWIFT TASK CONTINUATION MISUSE: start(launcher:interface:)\n38:   leaked its continuation` \u2014 UTM awaits macOS vmnet bridge creation forever\n39:   when the interface can't be bridged; manifests as an infinite spinner.\n40: \u002d Not fixable from our artifacts (NIC model irrelevant); mitigations: explicit\n\nTARGET 26 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_27\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY fe15ecbd8f55cd1e82f89b1d489662805f9f088a dba68e7a6febe1fd82db701659a16bd93d974505293ed19b826fc20b6d03a5cd RANGES [[1, 41]] MASKED [3, 6, 12, 13, 14, 16]\n1: # 2026\u002d07\u002d27 Work Log\n2: \n3: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n4: \n5: \u002d Grounded the \"drop our auth layer?\" question in rclone's own rc server\n6: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n7:   the web GUI's login form just replays it as HTTP basic auth, and the\n8:   login_token is base64(user:pass). Dropping it does not remove a prompt, it\n9:   removes the wall: unauthenticated rc allows inline remote definitions and\n10:   backend init that can execute commands. rclone itself logs \"It is\n11:   recommended to use web gui with auth\", and omitting the flags makes rclone\n12: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n13: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n14: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n15:   GUI itself), so the browser is pre\u002dauthenticated and the page's login form\n16: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n17:   manual typing.\n18: \n19: ## UTM bundles can advertise a reachable host address\n20: \n21: \u002d Problem: behind a port forward the guest cannot discover the address a phone\n22:   must scan, and no launcher runs on macOS to inject it (fw_cfg injection was\n23:   Linux\u002dlauncher\u002donly).\n24: \u002d Solution: the generated .utm bundle now ships the fw_cfg argument\n25:   pre\u002dwritten with a deliberately invalid placeholder\n26:   (EDIT\u002dME\u002dhttp://your\u002dhost\u002dip:15572). The tester edits it once in UTM's\n27:   QEMU > Additional Arguments; until then the guest rejects it and falls back\n28:   to its own address. Bridged bundles omit the argument (guest is on the LAN).\n29: \u002d 095\u002dcloud\u002durl quirk restructured so any invalid/placeholder value also\n30:   clears a stale override, not just a missing fw_cfg key.\n31: \u002d fw_cfg key and host port moved into profile.json (source of truth) and\n32:   shared by both the Linux launcher and the UTM bundle; profile bumped to v4.\n33: \u002d Verified by rendering both outputs: launcher emits the live host IP, bundle\n34:   emits the placeholder, port forwards and Emulated VLAN mode unchanged.\n35: \n36: ## Notes\n37: \n38: \u002d Issue #26 round\u002dtrip QA still awaiting maintainer results (no tracker\n39:   movement since 2026\u002d07\u002d26); both items above were the unblocked work.\n40: \u002d Changes are uncommitted: cloud_setup on feature/cloud\u002dsaves, VM tooling in\n\nTARGET 27 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_28\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY de6260755d21644c9f50827b58fcc556cdaacbee 4c61752db292091fec15b842bccc499547c581cfa3ff91c3fe9e045756ef7804 RANGES [[1, 41]] MASKED [16]\n1: # 2026\u002d07\u002d28 Work Log\n2: \n3: ## QA image 20260728 shipped with the two session\u002dend improvements\n4: \n5: \u002d Merged cloud_setup single\u002dprompt fix through test/qa\u002dintegration and the\n6:   VM advertisement work through test/qa\u002dgeneric\u002dx64; cleared rclone/quirks/\n7:   image stamps (script\u002donly changes don't trigger rebuilds); built and\n8:   published dev\u002dgeneric_x64\u002d20260728. First publish run was interrupted and\n9:   left the release as a draft \u2014 flipped to prerelease via gh release edit.\n10: \n11: ## Tester feedback: QR still dead, guest showed 10.0.x\n12: \n13: \u002d Root cause chain: placeholder edit is real friction; tester didn't do it,\n14:   fallback correctly showed the guest's own (unreachable) NAT address.\n15: \u002d Investigated alternatives before adding tooling:\n16: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n17:     user:pass@ userinfo is Android\u002donly sugar; the login_token query param\n18:     is what actually signs iPhones in (it's base64(user:pass), handled by\n19:     rclone's GUI, not the browser). Keep both.\n20:   \u002d In\u002dguest host discovery is impossible by construction: user\u002dmode NAT\n21:     exposes the host only as 10.0.2.2; no query returns its LAN address.\n22:   \u002d VirtualBox is a dead end: no x86_64 guests on Apple\u002dsilicon hosts\n23:     (virtualizer, not emulator), and its NAT has the same information\n24:     boundary anyway.\n25: \n26: ## One\u002dclick phone\u002dQR helper for macOS (set\u002dup\u002dphone\u002dqr.command)\n27: \n28: \u002d Bundle zip now carries an executable .command next to the .utm: detects\n29:   the Mac's LAN address (route \u002dn get default + ipconfig getifaddr),\n30:   rewrites the fw_cfg argument in config.plist via BSD sed, validates with\n31:   plutil. Idempotent; re\u002drun after network changes.\n32: \u002d Template lives in the VM dir; build fills @FWCFG_NAME@/@HOST_PORT@ from\n33:   profile.json so tooling can't drift from the profile. Exec bit set via\n34:   ZipInfo external_attr (0o100755<<16) \u2014 verified to survive unzip, and\n35:   macOS Archive Utility honors it. Gatekeeper: first run right\u002dclick>Open.\n36: \u002d Platform matrix documented in the VM README: Linux automatic (launcher),\n37:   macOS one double\u002dclick, Windows expected via WSL2 QEMU + Linux launcher\n38:   (plus netsh portproxy or mirrored networking) \u2014 deferred until a Windows\n39:   tester exists.\n40: \u002d Guest image unchanged (host\u002dside tooling only): republished the same\n\nTARGET 28 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_30\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 6be24bb11cf3f76eaa3f1ff45dda546f055172f5 6e310542aa66559044b52e4261fff815a5ac95600a58f7ad09eca884ae8f3a31 RANGES [[1, 31]] MASKED [13]\n1: # 2026\u002d07\u002d30 Work Log\n2: \n3: ## Cloud setup rebuilt around rclone's interactive config (web GUI retired)\n4: \n5: \u002d Tester verdict on the web GUI: worse than the CLI \u2014 never asked to\n6:   authenticate the backend or choose directories. Grounded why: the GUI's\n7:   config API is non\u002dinteractive by design (returns questions, cannot run\n8:   OAuth); rclone\u002dwebui\u002dreact is effectively unmaintained. A live probe of\n9:   the rc state machine confirmed OAuth stops at \"*oauth\u002dislocal\" needing a\n10:   browser on localhost:53682.\n11: \u002d Decision (user): wrap rclone's interactive config rather than rebuild a\n12:   web UI. cloud_setup now shows big\u002dtext SSH instructions (command +\n13: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n14:   \u002dL 53682:localhost:53682 tunnel so the provider sign\u002din opens in the\n15:   connecting computer's browser; optional ssh:// QR for phone SSH apps;\n16:   on return it VERIFIES the remote (rclone lsd with timeouts) and points\n17:   at `rclone config reconnect` when the sign\u002din didn't stick.\n18: \u002d The whole VM address\u002ddiscovery apparatus collapsed: the loopback SSH\n19:   command is a fixed string on every host platform, so both launchers\n20:   inject it via fw_cfg (opt/org.rocknix.cloud_ssh), the quirk became\n21:   095\u002dcloud\u002dssh (also cleans the retired cloud_setup_url), and the macOS\n22:   helper script + Gatekeeper dance + web\u002dGUI port forward are gone.\n23:   Profile v5. Solves Linux/macOS/Windows\u002dvia\u002dWSL2 uniformly.\n24: \u002d Commits: f34d8c1ce1 (feature/cloud\u002dsaves), ffa3ca5b8a\n25:   (feature/generic\u002dx64); merged through test/qa\u002dintegration into\n26:   test/qa\u002dgeneric\u002dx64; image rebuilt; dev\u002dgeneric_x64\u002d20260729 published\n27:   and verified (SSH instructions in image, no helper in bundle).\n28: \u002d Follow\u002dups filed: #28 (ES\u002dnative remote picker + sync path settings, so\n29:   SSH shrinks to just the provider sign\u002din), #29 (upstream OAuth device\n30:   flow to rclone \u2014 the elegant end state).\n\nTARGET 29 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_08\u002dwork_logs/2026_08_01\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 9e313511996b65dbb2b1f8c351602daa5596b2d3 17882950cd8ed723d1b2182508178179440c50573965c44c020df8bacbda55b2 RANGES [[1, 41]] MASKED [9, 26, 31]\n1: # 2026\u002d08\u002d01 Work Log\n2: \n3: ## UTM boot failure: whitespace in AdditionalArguments\n4: