ts\n33:   route to it. (06102aa36, feature/cloud\u002dsync\u002dmenu; ES pin bumped to\n34:   62ad0386c on test/qa\u002dintegration)\n35: \u002d The ssh:// QR code is gone with the console screen \u002d it was a phone\n36:   SSH\u002dapp convenience only; the flow targets a computer. If wanted\n37:   later, ES has image\u002ddisplay components (GuiImageViewer precedent) but\n38:   it needs a QR rasterizer in ES \u002d not worth it now.\n39: \u002d Rebuilt with ES pin bump + rclone stamps cleared, republished\n40:   dev\u002dgeneric_x64\u002d20260802; verified image ships cloud_setup \u002d\u002dinfo and\n\nTARGET 30 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_08\u002dwork_logs/2026_08_14\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY d925ec584851c3835cc81f3f2f786e0e3f3690a6 52ab9ccd5d5597ac208a47c0cf8c087e20c016bd1464d27996bf1f47a31b8a37 RANGES [[1, 41]] MASKED [20, 21, 26, 27]\n1: # 2026\u002d08\u002d14 Work Log\n2: \n3: ## Same\u002dtag republish caused a stale\u002dbuild test (8/2)\n4: \n5: \u002d Tester saw no native cloud\u002dsetup page in \"the 8/2 build\". Root cause:\n6:   dev\u002dgeneric_x64\u002d20260802 was published twice under the same tag and\n7:   filename \u2014 first at ~01:00 UTC (UTM whitespace fix only), then\n8:   republished at ~05:50\u002d06:25 UTC after the native ES page merged.\n9:   A copy downloaded between the two publishes (or a UTM VM imported\n10:   from the early zip \u2014 UTM copies the bundle on import) boots the old\n11:   flow. Verified: the only local 20260802 build (stamps 05:47\u002d05:50)\n12:   and the current release assets are the complete cut.\n13: \u002d Takeaway: a same\u002dday respin under an identical tag/filename is\n14:   indistinguishable to the tester. Prefer a fresh date tag (as today)\n15:   or a `\u002dr2` suffix; compare the asset sha256 when in doubt.\n16: \n17: ## Cloud setup: checklist page reworked into a gated wizard\n18: \n19: \u002d Tester feedback on the native page: it was a checklist, not a flow \u2014\n20: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n21: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n22:   shown regardless of scenario, and nothing enforcing the mandatory steps.\n23: \u002d Now a three\u002dstep wizard; mandatory steps are *verified*, never\n24:   skippable, only exitable (every gate offers EXIT SETUP):\n25:   \u002d Step 1 CONNECT: how to connect (same network, terminal, exact\n26: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n27: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n28:     SSH. Gate: `cloud_setup \u002d\u002dconnected` must see an established\n29:     inbound SSH session (read from `/proc/net/tcp*`, port 22/state 01 \u2014\n30:     no ss/netstat dependency).\n31:   \u002d Step 2 CONFIGURE: rclone\u002dconfig instructions branched by scenario\n32:     (first remote / add another / repair\u002dmodify with reconnect wording).\n33:     Gate: `cloud_setup \u002d\u002dcheck` must verify the remote. In add\u002danother\n34:     mode the gate diffs the remote list against wizard start and checks\n35:     the remote that was actually added \u2014 a working pre\u002dexisting remote\n36:     cannot wave the step through.\n37:   \u002d Step 3 DONE: confirmation + clearly optional immediate backup.\n38:   \u002d Entry point branches: no remotes \u2192 \"SET UP YOUR FIRST REMOTE\"\n39:     wizard; otherwise a chooser (per\u002dremote check / add / repair).\n40: \u002d Script contract (rclone e61fa9cac2): `\u002d\u002dconnected` (new gate),\n"
